          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 00:18:53.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-04 02:25:16.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: shorten obd_timeout in replay-dual",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: shorten obd_timeout in replay-dual\n\nreplay-dual loses a client before a failover in 0a, 0b, 15a,\n15c, 16, 17, 20 (twice) and 21a, and each recovery waits for\nit until the timer expires. Client reconnects extend the timer\nto their service estimate plus a margin that scales with\nobd_timeout, about 20 seconds shorter at 10 than at 20.\n\nreplay-dual was left at the full timeout because the hard\nlimit, 9 * obd_timeout, is then 90 seconds. After test_18 the\nclients' service estimates are high enough that the extended\ntimer of test_20 and test_21a reaches it, and the hard limit\naborts recovery and evicts the client still replaying:\ntest_21a fails, and 26, 30 and 31 after it.\n\nMount the targets with recovery_time_hard at 9 times the\nsuite's starting TIMEOUT, which is the default hard limit, and\ncall set_recovery_timeout. The recovery of test_21a then ends\nat 90 seconds by evicting only the lost client.\n\nFull replay-dual, 2 MDTs, 2 OSTs, 2 clients, two runs on each\ntree: 1767 to 1387 seconds on average, with the same passes and\nskips. About 730 hours of CI per 30 days over the three review\ngroups that run it.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=replay-dual\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=replay-dual\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ic12e37a77691a999fe5337086ee3e162480a51ea\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
